# Carrot Note App — Improvement Plan

Use this rule when implementing features, refactors, or UX polish. Prioritize phases in order unless the user scopes a single area.

## Current State (baseline)

- **Stack:** Expo 51, React Native, Firebase Auth + Firestore, React Navigation, react-native-paper, reanimated
- **Screens:** Loading → Calendar (home), NoteList, NoteDetail, Settings, Login/Signup
- **Data model:** Single flat `Note` type (`title`, `note`, `completed`, `category`, `startDate`, `endDate`)
- **Themes:** light, darkGreen, darkTeal via `ThemeContext`
- **Pain points:** No Firestore real-time sync; duplicated fetch/category logic in `NoteList` + `CalendarScreen`; inline header styles; limited test coverage; README still describes generic todo scaffold

---

## Phase 1 — Logic & Architecture (foundation)

Do this before new note types so extensions don't multiply tech debt.

### 1.1 Real-time Firestore listeners
- Replace one-shot `fetchNotes` + manual refresh with `onSnapshot` in a shared hook
- Unsubscribe on blur/unmount to avoid leaks
- Keep pull-to-refresh as a forced re-sync fallback

```typescript
// Target: app/hooks/useNotes.ts
export function useNotes(userId: string | undefined) {
  // onSnapshot → notes[], loading, error, refresh()
}
```

### 1.2 Shared data hooks
Extract duplicated logic from `NoteList.tsx` and `CalendarScreen.tsx`:
- `useNotes(userId)` — notes + loading + error
- `useCategories(userId)` — categories + seed defaults (`Home`, `Shopping`)
- `useNoteFilters(notes)` — category filter, completion filter, search

### 1.3 Centralized note mutations
- Wrap `addNote`, `updateNote`, `toggleStatus`, `deleteNote` in a `noteActions` module or context
- Always pair delete with `cancelDeadlineReminder`
- Always pair date changes with `upsertDeadlineReminder` / `cancelDeadlineReminder`
- Surface errors via a single `showError(message)` helper instead of scattered `Alert.alert`

### 1.4 Optimistic UI
- Toggle complete / delete: update local state immediately, rollback on Firestore failure
- Reduces perceived lag on slow networks

### 1.5 Type-safe navigation params
- Ensure `Detail` receives `noteId` (not full `Note` object) so edits on one screen reflect everywhere
- Fetch or select from store by id to avoid stale route params

