## Phase 2 — UI Improvements

Match existing design tokens in `app/theme/ui.ts` and `themes.ts`. Do not introduce a second design system.

### 2.1 Shared UI primitives
Create small reusable components under `app/components/ui/`:
- `ScreenHeaderActions` — calendar + settings pills (currently duplicated inline)
- `CategoryChipRow` — horizontal filter chips with count badges
- `EmptyState` — icon, title, subtitle, optional CTA
- `LoadingState` — consistent spinner + message
- `Card` — surface + border + shadow wrapper

### 2.2 Note list UX
- **Search bar** above category chips (filter by title + note body)
- **Sort options:** newest, oldest, due date, category
- **Completion filter:** All / Active / Completed
- **Inline complete** checkbox on `NoteItem` (avoid navigating to Detail for simple toggles)
- **Category color dots** on each row (store color on category doc in Firestore)
- **Haptic feedback** on swipe-delete and complete (expo-haptics)

### 2.3 Calendar screen UX
- Dot indicators on calendar days (count or color by category)
- "Today" quick-jump button
- Week view toggle (optional, phase 2b)
- Unify QuickAdd + NoteDetail field layout for consistency

### 2.4 Note detail UX
- Character count for title/body
- Sticky action bar (Update / Complete / Delete) on scroll
- Unsaved-changes guard on back navigation
- Better date picker affordance (show human-readable "Due in 2 days")

### 2.5 Auth & settings polish
- Password visibility toggle on Login/Signup
- App version + build number in Settings footer
- Confirm dialog before logout
- Respect system color scheme as a 4th theme option (`system` → light/darkGreen/darkTeal)

### 2.6 Accessibility
- `accessibilityLabel` on swipe actions, filter chips, FAB
- Minimum 44pt touch targets
- Screen reader announcements on complete/delete

### 2.7 Motion
- Subtle list item enter animation (FadeInDown via reanimated)
- Spring on filter chip selection
- Keep animations under 300ms; respect reduced-motion where possible

